Z||000000||beachbomb||05-28-2000||08:47 PM||||Hi all! I am still having tach probs. My tach reads about 1500-2000 higher than engine is actually doing. i have looked but cannot locate the tach filter that the Service manual says the car is suppose to have. i have traced the white wire coming off the distributor to the back fire wall and there is no tach filter there. Is this the right wire? What does the tach filter look like? Could it be another prob? ANy help would be greatly appreciated. This problem is just annoying!! thanks alot..jim<BR>p.s. Car is a 1984 Indy Fiero.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||05-28-2000||09:39 PM||||I don't know where the tach filter is on the four cylinder engine, but on the V-6 its next to the distributor and its a little round silver cannister about the size of a Bic lighter with two wires coming out of it. It is attached to the engine block by a clamp. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnnyK||05-28-2000||10:34 PM||||On the 4 cylinder it is to the right of the distributor, mounted somewhere above the tranny if I remember correctly.. Really small, and has blue caps on the ends (but mine was rusted beyond recognition, as I'm sure yours is too).. Mine had a plug so I could easily disconnect it, but upon going to the junkyard there, all of them (6-7) had filters with no plugs, and wires just going straight to the other wires so they are unaccessible.. Maybe I'm just lucky..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
